{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533045-how-clement-lupus-showcases-w5-s-biggest-flaw","id":1533045,"title":"How Clement Lupus showcases W5's biggest flaw","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-23T13:45:38-07:00","id":1533045,"title":"How Clement Lupus showcases W5's biggest flaw","content":"<b>WARNING: This essay discusses topics such as bestiality, sexual abuse of an intellectually disabled creature, animal death and some darker aspects of domestication. PLEASE do not read unless you can handle these topics.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> One of the enduring critiques of WtA over the years has been its inclusion of the lupus breed. To some people, the fact that the garou can breed with wolves is a bridge too far. It would not be a problem, but many times these people will come to spaces discussing WtA and call breeding with wolves \u201cdoggy rape.\u201d Which sours a discussion fast.<br /> <br /> What these people do not grasp, is that all garou can communicate with wolves just fine. They can ask for consent from the wolf and the wolf can give informed consent back. That used to be the end of the matter.<br /> <br /> Until W5 came around.<br /> <br /> From the previews alone, we were told that the wolf form and the giant monster wolf form can be mistaken for dogs. It was met with amusement, as wolves alone tower over any sort of wolf-like dog breed. Nevermind the monster wolf form of hispo which is a wolf tank. All of this was met with humour.<br /> <br /> Until someone noted there was a merit that made you look like a dog.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>W5 p.98</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clement Lupus: Your lupus form appears more dog-like than wolf-like, and unless they have a reason to believe so, no human onlooker who sees you in lupus form thinks that you\u2019re a wolf</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The last sentence is the lynchpin here. \u201cNo human onlooker who sees you in lupus form thinks that you are a wolf.\u201d The problem with this sentence is, that many huskies and agouti german shepherd dogs are thought to be wolves by ignorant people. There have been many loose dogs shot as 'wolves', the opposite of what was intended.<br /> <br /> It is effortless for an ST to declare that the lupus-form of a character with this merit looks like a golden retriever.<br /> <br /> What takes this from a silly merit to something a bit more serious, is the fact that wolf born are still in W5. Merits like this in Werewolf the Forsaken work, because there is no actual wolf heritage involved. But in W5, wolf born garou exist and since this merit is not a magical power but the actual physical appearance of the lupus form, it brings up a lot of uncomfortable questions.<br /> <br /> At the start of the essay, I said that garou can communicate with wolves and so ask informed consent from them. This is possible, because an adult wolf is truly an adult of their species. A dog, however, is mentally around a 4 month old wolf.<br /> <br /> Among wolves, a year old wolf is still an immature teenager as wolves are mature at 2 years. So a 4 month old wolf is truly a child in wolf terms and therefore in the terms of garou. A garou trying to breed with a dog is truly the \u201cdoggy rape\u201d people accused Legacy version of WtA of.<br /> <br /> And W5 just made that canon.<br /> <br /> <b>Please note, I do not think the authors intentionally made this gaff.</b> W5 is written often with only the human born garou in mind, with the wolf born included very rarely. The book even tells you not to have more animal Touchstones than one, because the game is focused on garou relations with humans. But this mistake truly showcases where W5 flounders. Aspects are included but not thought out well, such as giving no mechanical ability to have a custom patron, the book contradicting itself and so on.<br /> <br /> The idea of allowing garou to take on a dog-like form is not bad, there is a gift called \u201cGuise of the Hound\u201d which does that. What makes Clement Lupus such a bad idea is that it is not a power the garou uses but the garou's actual lupus form.<br /> <br /> This was a darker essay, but I hope it was informative.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 03-23-2024, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-23T18:17:11-07:00","id":1533055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533045-how-clement-lupus-showcases-w5-s-biggest-flaw#post1533045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the start of the essay, I said that garou can communicate with wolves and so ask informed consent from them. This is possible, because an adult wolf is truly an adult of their species. A dog, however, is mentally around a 4 month old wolf.<br /> <br /> Among wolves, a year old wolf is still an immature teenager as wolves are mature at 2 years. So a 4 month old wolf is truly a child in wolf terms and therefore in the terms of garou. A garou trying to breed with a dog is truly the \u201cdoggy rape\u201d people accused Legacy version of WtA of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so I'm a bit confused by the logic here.<br /> <br /> Apparently adult dogs are less mentally mature than adult wolves. So the suggestion here is that while an adult wolf could consent to sex with a werewolf a dog can't. And the &quot;Clement Lupus&quot; Merit makes normal humans assume that the werewolf in wolf form is a dog. <br /> <br /> So okay, I guess those are the pieces of the puzzle? But where is the idea that werewolves are canonically breeding with dogs coming from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-23T22:26:59-07:00","id":1533065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533045-how-clement-lupus-showcases-w5-s-biggest-flaw?p=1533055#post1533055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so I'm a bit confused by the logic here.<br /> <br /> Apparently adult dogs are less mentally mature than adult wolves. So the suggestion here is that while an adult wolf could consent to sex with a werewolf a dog can't. And the &quot;Clement Lupus&quot; Merit makes normal humans assume that the werewolf in wolf form is a dog.<br /> <br /> So okay, I guess those are the pieces of the puzzle? But where is the idea that werewolves are canonically breeding with dogs coming from?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only way a wolf born garou would have those doggy traits, is if they have VERY recent dog-ancestry. Because Clement Lupus is not a magical power but the actual looks of the garou, the only way for doggy traits to be there is if the garou ACTUALLY has dog in them.<br /> <br /> Which is why I think this was an oversight, the writer of that merit forgot lupus garou were still in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T00:35:30-07:00","id":1533069,"title":"","content":"Reading the merit, I assumed that the character's wolf form was simply small enough, and maybe had a superficial trait, such that someone seeing it could confuse it for a large generic dog rather than jump to the idea that they were dealing with a wolf.<br /> <br /> I don't imagine that anyone would be confusing the wolf for a specific breed of dog - definitely no were-chihuahuas or anything like that.<br /> <br /> So it seems like a bit of a stretch to me that this merit means that they werewolves are going around having sex with dogs. I mean, I guess it's possible, new edition and all but I don't think that's the intent of the merit, and I'm not really agreeing with the implication, let alone that this is now &quot;canon&quot; to W5.<br /> <br /> More likely, maybe a character's wolf-ancestor atv some point bred with a dog and that's where that trait came from","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T01:29:29-07:00","id":1533070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533045-how-clement-lupus-showcases-w5-s-biggest-flaw?p=1533069#post1533069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading the merit, I assumed that the character's wolf form was simply small enough, and maybe had a superficial trait, such that someone seeing it could confuse it for a large generic dog rather than jump to the idea that they were dealing with a wolf.<br /> <br /> I don't imagine that anyone would be confusing the wolf for a specific breed of dog - definitely no were-chihuahuas or anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolf content is pretty easy to see even wolf-dogs who are multiple generations removed;<br /> <br /> <img width=\"342\" height=\"458\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://64.media.tumblr.com/2048b4e43570d51d8ff5b19a5cebc3ab/3fcadb400c0cf0af-8b/s2048x3072/82fd465674a648ea214dab6d42fb7755728ea8ec.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://64.media.tumblr.com/2048b4e43570d51d8ff5b19a5cebc3ab/3fcadb400c0cf0af-8b/s2048x3072/82fd465674a648ea214dab6d42fb7755728ea8ec.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://64.media.tumblr.com/2048b4e43570d51d8ff5b19a5cebc3ab/3fcadb400c0cf0af-8b/s2048x3072/82fd465674a648ea214dab6d42fb7755728ea8ec.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> This is Zephyr with her 1 year old son Druid. Druid's father was an Alaskan Husky so he has more dog content than his mother has. He still clearly looks wolfish.<br /> <br /> The problem with mistaking a wolf for a generic dog is that wolves are way WAYY bigger than regular dogs and most have markings that are indistinct compared the a dog's. You can't even mistake a dingo for a regular dog. This is why in Legacy, only high content wolf-dogs could be garou. Aka, there was no mistaking them for dogs. While I don't think the intention was of a were-chihuahua, the statement still indicates the character looks more dog than wolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533045-how-clement-lupus-showcases-w5-s-biggest-flaw?p=1533069#post1533069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it seems like a bit of a stretch to me that this merit means that they werewolves are going around having sex with dogs. I mean, I guess it's possible, new edition and all but I don't think that's the intent of the merit, and I'm not really agreeing with the implication, let alone that this is now &quot;canon&quot; to W5.<br /> <br /> More likely, maybe a character's wolf-ancestor atv some point bred with a dog and that's where that trait came from</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing, I don't think this was the intent, either. I am pretty sure the intent was that the character looks doggy and so gets overlooked. The issue is that whoever wrote that merit and whoever wrote that both lupus AND hispo forms look like 'big dogs' did not do the needed research to understand what the text implied. It is very likely they forgot that the wolf born were a thing in W5 and just assumed the character's lupus form had no longer lineage of wolves than that. That would have been fine.<br /> <br /> But wolf born ARE a thing in W5 and as that merit is not magical and it states you cannot be mistaken for a wolf, the conclusion is that the wolf born had very recent dog ancestry. And given werewolf lineage MIGHT be a thing in W5, you can fill in the rest.<br /> <br /> Again, I am 100% certain breeding with dogs was not the intention. But this lack of forethought in that merit is an aspect that is shown in many aspects of W5, something is brought up but not given further thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 03-24-2024, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T02:02:01-07:00","id":1533071,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the text that says that ' no human onlooker who sees you in lupus form thinks that you\u2019re a wolf' is........troubling cos there are millions of people out there who think a husky or malamute......or an alsatian......looks like a wolf. SO for that to apply to Clement Lupus they must be so utterly dog-like that <u>no human onlooker </u>thinks they are a wolf so that eliminates all wolf-dogs, coy-dogs and &quot; wolf like&quot; breeds it also eliminates a whole bunch of spitz types, a wide selection of shepherds and the like.<br /> <br /> Which gets a little........odd.........perhaps they actually meant to write ' no human onlooker who knows what a wolf looks like' but we know they didn't because Clement Lupus is intended to be used so that animal control doesn't immediately attend whenever a Pack heads out with a member in Lupus form....so they have to look SO dog-like that that will never occur.<br /> <br /> Add to this that all Clement Lupus ( which is a VERY popular merit) in AP games I've seen are either played as Tik-tok star dogs, the family pet or a kind of canine Mrs Doubtfire and its just a tad icky even before we get to HOW did a wolf end up looking like a generic dog if they didn't come from breeding with mans best friend.<br /> <br /> As Ana said I think they just went ' people want to play dogs not wolves' lets do that and didn't really think any further on it.... <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T02:16:14-07:00","id":1533072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533045-how-clement-lupus-showcases-w5-s-biggest-flaw?p=1533071#post1533071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Add to this that all Clement Lupus ( which is a VERY popular merit) in AP games I've seen are either played as Tik-tok star dogs, the family pet or a kind of canine Mrs Doubtfire and its just a tad icky even before we get to HOW did a wolf end up looking like a generic dog if they didn't come from breeding with mans best friend.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>AP games?<br /> <br /> And also, yeeesh. All of those are creepy af, especially the family pet. Keeping wolf-dogs is insanely hard, because they (obviously) are very clever and independent. Someone owning a wolf-dog would notice if their wolf-dog started going missing and suddenly got VERY aggressive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T07:31:54-07:00","id":1533076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533045-how-clement-lupus-showcases-w5-s-biggest-flaw?p=1533072#post1533072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> AP games?<br /> <br /> And also, yeeesh. All of those are creepy af, especially the family pet. Keeping wolf-dogs is insanely hard, because they (obviously) are very clever and independent. Someone owning a wolf-dog would notice if their wolf-dog started going missing and suddenly got VERY aggressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actual Play. ( On Youtube, Podcasts and such.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T09:18:38-07:00","id":1533077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533045-how-clement-lupus-showcases-w5-s-biggest-flaw?p=1533076#post1533076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actual Play. ( On Youtube, Podcasts and such.)</div> </div> </div> </div>...Wow. So people put out their Weredog RPs with no irony XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T09:33:46-07:00","id":1533078,"title":"","content":"You are talking about therians?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T10:14:40-07:00","id":1533080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533045-how-clement-lupus-showcases-w5-s-biggest-flaw?p=1533078#post1533078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are talking about therians?</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, no......well, maybe in their spare time. But we are currently referring to streamed roleplaying sessions of the game W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T11:15:04-07:00","id":1533081,"title":"","content":"I think most have more taste than that and more understanding of how an actual wolf thinks. Ugh. TikTok star dogs. That's exactly the kind of shit you do <i>not</i> want to incentivize people to do with lupus characters. The doggification of lupus is just gross.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T12:42:13-07:00","id":1533084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533045-how-clement-lupus-showcases-w5-s-biggest-flaw?p=1533081#post1533081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think most have more taste than that and more understanding of how an actual wolf thinks. Ugh. TikTok star dogs. That's exactly the kind of shit you do <i>not</i> want to incentivize people to do with lupus characters. The doggification of lupus is just gross.</div> </div> </div> </div>More than that, the lupus breed is there to be a reminder that the garou mission is NOT just limited to humans. A dog is at best a feral creature, not a wild animal.<br /> <br /> The whole thing is gross, from the implications to.... that stuff. Especially as Legacy made a point to note that only high content wolf-dogs can become garou outside wolves and dingo, and the only way to look like a doggy dog? A rank 3 gift of the Bone Gnawers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T13:26:24-07:00","id":1533085,"title":"","content":"I think that Merit highlights an even bigger issue in W5: What about wolfborn Garou and wolf-Kin? W5 would certainly work better if wolf-born Garou and wolf-Kin wouldn't be a thing. Clearly, nobody gave a shit about that aspect while writing the released W5 corebook. Although it gets really weird with something like the Red Talon Tribe where a lot of the aggressiveness and sociopathy is kept while the main-trait of the Tribe (its wolf-born-only membership) is removed. Another sign of how little attention has been paid to that aspect of WtA.<br /> <br /> As for the merit, I could imagine someone just thinking of an equivalent to a Merit that makes it easier for a vampire to pass as a human and this being the result of that thought-exercise. Not a good result, mind you. But it wouldn't surprise me to find out that this team of people who worked on this final version of W5 that was released ended up looking in all the wrong corners and obsessed over the wrong questions when they were tasked to update WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T13:46:00-07:00","id":1533087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533045-how-clement-lupus-showcases-w5-s-biggest-flaw?p=1533085#post1533085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the merit, I could imagine someone just thinking of an equivalent to a Merit that makes it easier for a vampire to pass as a human and this being the result of that thought-exercise. Not a good result, mind you. But it wouldn't surprise me to find out that this team of people who worked on this final version of W5 that was released ended up looking in all the wrong corners and obsessed over the wrong questions when they were tasked to update WtA.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does kind of go against the fantasy of a werewolf, though. While the wolf born are clearly ignored as much as possible, you'd think players would still want to play a scary wolf and not a dog. Or are the players fine with only crinos being scary?<br /> <br /> I do find the popularity of that merit darkly funny, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T14:28:57-07:00","id":1533090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533045-how-clement-lupus-showcases-w5-s-biggest-flaw?p=1533087#post1533087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does kind of go against the fantasy of a werewolf, though. While the wolf born are clearly ignored as much as possible, you'd think players would still want to play a scary wolf and not a dog. Or are the players fine with only crinos being scary?<br /> <br /> I do find the popularity of that merit darkly funny, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think WtF is better at justifying the five Forms, to begin with. That would certainly be something I would've stolen if someone had put me in charge of a new edition of WtA. What we got in the released version is that the main-reason to shapeshift is that most Gifts can only be used in supernatural Forms. And the Rage-Check-requirement means it's more likely you're gonna shift because you wanna do combat and then really only the Crinos-Form makes sense. Other than that, using other Forms is super-situational and considering it's reliant on Rage-checks, it's not like the system encourages players to delve into that part of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T18:00:05-07:00","id":1533099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533045-how-clement-lupus-showcases-w5-s-biggest-flaw?p=1533085#post1533085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the merit, I could imagine someone just thinking of an equivalent to a Merit that makes it easier for a vampire to pass as a human and this being the result of that thought-exercise. Not a good result, mind you. But it wouldn't surprise me to find out that this team of people who worked on this final version of W5 that was released ended up looking in all the wrong corners and obsessed over the wrong questions when they were tasked to update WtA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly If I was writing the merit, I would make it clear it's a magical equivalent of someone else's problem field from Hitch hikers guide to the galaxy. If only because large parts of my setting is such a an urban hellscape that most people living in it won't regard a dog as pettable but good source of non-rat protein. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T00:58:37-07:00","id":1533108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533045-how-clement-lupus-showcases-w5-s-biggest-flaw?p=1533099#post1533099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly If I was writing the merit, I would make it clear it's a magical equivalent of someone else's problem field from Hitch hikers guide to the galaxy. If only because large parts of my setting is such a an urban hellscape that most people living in it won't regard a dog as pettable but good source of non-rat protein.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, given W5 IS set during the Apocalypse, you'd think so. But nah, instagram star.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T01:06:04-07:00","id":1533110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533045-how-clement-lupus-showcases-w5-s-biggest-flaw?p=1533108#post1533108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, given W5 IS set during the Apocalypse, you'd think so. But nah, instagram star.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I guess that some syndicate would like to ransom a fancy dog but in the back streets food is food. Hell people won't be disturbed if a &quot;dog&quot; they killed suddenly become a human corpse. Hell in sector 23's street of flavor it would god send since the chefs pay good ahn for fresh ingredients...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":".  grammar 03-25-2024, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T14:24:33-07:00","id":1533138,"title":"","content":"So some early lurches into the Apocalypse and everything goes full on CyberRealm Slums/Wicked City? Because that usually only happens in broken mirrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T20:31:38-07:00","id":1533150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533045-how-clement-lupus-showcases-w5-s-biggest-flaw?p=1533138#post1533138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So some early lurches into the Apocalypse and everything goes full on CyberRealm Slums/Wicked City? Because that usually only happens in broken mirrors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no the the Apocalypse has long past in my setting... Well Apocalypse to be more accurate since in my setting's back story <b>ALL </b>the gamelines Apocalypse happened near simultaneously, the wrym and weaver fighting each other, all the Antediluvians awaken, ect, ect. <br /> <br /> The only reason there's still a earth to live on is because all of the said threats have mutually offed them selves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T22:37:50-07:00","id":1533155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533045-how-clement-lupus-showcases-w5-s-biggest-flaw?p=1533150#post1533150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh no the the Apocalypse has long past in my setting... Well Apocalypse to be more accurate since in my setting's back story <b>ALL </b>the gamelines Apocalypse happened near simultaneously, the wrym and weaver fighting each other, all the Antediluvians awaken, ect, ect.<br /> <br /> The only reason there's still a earth to live on is because all of the said threats have mutually offed them selves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cosmic forces clashing are a bit more... influential on events than mere 3rd gens waking up. Like, if the Wyrm and Weaver actually manage to kill each other, only the Wyld exists, which means that existence becomes a lot more... transient. Certainly, it'd be completely unrelatable to what we know as existence, life, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}